  "description": "Parses the 51Degrees device identifier (51Did) returned by the 51Degrees Cloud service. The 51Did is an OWID envelope (the identifier) whose payload carries a 1-byte flags bit-mask (usage tier and identifier type), a 4-byte little-endian License Id, and the identifier value: a 32-byte SHA-256 for probabilistic and hashed-email identifiers or 16 GUID bytes for random ones. Compare probabilistic values, never full identifiers: two 51Dids for the same device share the same value even though their envelopes differ on every issue. The FodId type inherits from Owid.Client.Model.Owid (SWAN-community/owid-dotnet) and unpacks those three payload fields.",
